  "verbalization": "Euparotin is linked to SNB-78 through a series of molecular targets, with Caspase-5 acting as a central mediator. The evidence suggests that Euparotin targets Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid and Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of Caspase-5, which is a key enzyme in the extrinsic and intrinsic pathways of apoptosis. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Caspase-5 supports the idea that Euparotin may act through a similar mechanism, potentially modulating apoptosis-related processes. The relationship between Euparotin and SNB-78 is thus supported by the shared involvement of Caspase-5 in the target network, with the exact mechanism of interaction likely involving the regulation of apoptosis through this enzyme.",
